id=snap-daily
name=snap-daily
version=v1.6
versionCode=7
author=pantha704
description=05:00 IST camera snap. Installs scripts + crond. Not an LSPosed hook. Daily decision is IST-checked in watch.sh, never a cron hour. v1.2: retry cap, retry window, battery floor, one-snap-per-day sent guard, PIN self-heal, crond watchdog. v1.3: attempts confined to the 05:00-06:00 IST window, Snapchat closed after the day is done so the camera is not left warm, keepalive that re-raises tailscaled / adb 5555 / ssh / wifi from the crond heartbeat, post-fs-data second boot stage. v1.4: unlock by clearing the PIN and swiping instead of restarting SystemUI, which is what left the notification shade stuck open over the keyguard (snap failed 10-05 and 10-06 with "no shutter [focus=NotificationShade]"); shade handling in the wait loop as a fallback. v1.5: watch.sh now logs every beat to logs/watch_<date>.log, runs run.sh without exec so a non-zero exit is caught and alerted, and the silence alarm fires when the window closes with no sent_ marker even if an attempt ran (the old condition hid exactly that case, which is how 2026-11-07..13 failed silently). v1.6: set -eu in snap.sh (line 4) combined with an unguarded settings write (line 182) meant ONE dropped binder call aborted the whole run before Snapchat was touched — no photo, no queue, no retry, no alert. All blind system calls are now failure-guarded and verified instead of assumed. queue_reason() only retried stuck:/no * since v1.2, so input/settings errors never queued and the retry path was unreachable; it now matches them. The attempt gate moved from ran_$today (created by the first attempt, so permanently false) to sent_$today plus tries < MAX_TRIES, giving 3 attempts inside the window. wake() verifies mWakefulness and that screen_off_timeout actually reached 180000 — it was silently staying 30000 and the display slept mid-run, after which every tap hit a dark screen (mCurrentFocus=null). wait_landmark now wakes a sleeping display, tap_line reports real injection status and retries (15x2s), tap_until re-fires the shutter until the preview appears, and Back is gated on Snapchat owning the foreground so it cannot walk out to the launcher.
